    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Qr1xZqYxtFr8AZmzgy17Dp)_\n\n## Summary\nFixes `Error running timer 'vulpea-ui--run-scheduled-sync': (wrong-type-argument vulpea-note nil)`.\n\nThe sidebar sync renders the backlinks widget, which calls `vulpea-ui-backlinks-note-filter` with the note of each linking file. That note is nil when the file is not in the vulpea database yet (new, unsynced or untracked file, as happens around the `sp-org-tag-` commands that open or create files). Our filter called `vulpea-note-tags` on it. It now keeps such files.\n\nChanged in the org source (`docs/tangles/vulpea/sp-vulpea.org`) and the tangled `sp-vulpea-ui.el` identically, plus a CHANGELOG entry.\n\n## Testing\nNot run: no Emacs in the container, and the filter is an inline `use-package` option, so no ERT test. The cause was read from the installed vulpea-ui source (`vulpea-ui--backlinks` calls the filter with `file-note`, which can be nil).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi94n3HDQ7YUU9pLdBV)_",
